@startuml SandboxBackend
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Sandbox backend — first-class for claudecode + cursor;\ndocker+egress stays as the fallback path

component "doRun backend selection\n""man.IsSbx() && mode != review""\n&& ""internal/sbx.Available()""" as SEL <<app>>
component "internal/sbx\nAvailable · WriteKit · SecretSet\nRunArgs · RemoveArgs" as SBX <<app>>
component "sbx CLI (v0.35 pre-GA)\nrun --kit … / secret set / rm" as CLI <<host>>
component "Kit spec.yaml (per run)\nallowedDomains = manifest hosts ∪\nprovider endpoints ∪ PROVEO_EGRESS_PROVIDER_DOMAINS" as KIT <<app>>
component "host-side credential injection\nvalues via stdin — never argv,\nnever env, never the VM fs" as SEC <<error>>

component "docker+egress orchestration\nnets · Squid · MITM inspector" as FB <<host>>

SEL ARROW_MAIN SBX : available
SEL ARROW_QUEUE FB : unavailable → one actionable warn
SBX ARROW_MAIN CLI
SBX ..> KIT : rendered under state egDir/sbx/kit
SBX ..> SEC

note right of SEL
  **Auto w/ fallback, one operator override.** Harnesses with
  ""docker: sbx"" (""claudecode"", ""cursor"") take the sandbox backend
  whenever the host supports it. The choice prompt carries it as the
  CHECKED add-on ""docker (sandbox)"" — unchecking is the one way to send
  such a run down docker+egress instead, and the answer is remembered
  per harness like every other axis. Unsupported hosts
  (no sbx on PATH, or no Apple Silicon / KVM) fall back to docker+egress
  with a single warn naming the reason. ""--print"" renders whichever
  backend was selected (""sbx run …"" vs ""docker run ..."").
end note

note right of SBX
  **Availability gate** (all must hold):
  | sbx CLI on PATH
  | darwin/arm64, **or** linux with ""/dev/kvm""
  Win11/Hyper-V and Intel macs are not gated in yet.
  The review tier is greyed out in the picker when this backend is
  selected — the consent-gate socket has no sbx transport yet.
end note

note bottom of SEC
  **Credential parity with the broker, different mechanism.** Declared secret
  env vars plus every detected provider key var are injected via ""sbx secret
  set"" before the run; the sentinel/broker-file machinery of the egress path
  is deliberately not involved — deny-by-default egress replaces interception.
  Accepted gap: no DLP content scan on payloads to *allowed* hosts.
end note

note left of FB
  **Fallback contract:** open-source harnesses (""opencode"", ""cecli"") never set
  ""docker: sbx"" (they take ""docker: dind"") and always run here. Subscription
  harnesses land here only
  when the gate above fails. Def-local shell suites keep covering the fallback
  images; ""tests/e2e/sbx_test.go"" skips unless the host can run sbx.

  **Plan vs proof.** The print-only tests assert the ARGV (pure ""sandboxSpec"",
  no VM). ""TestSandboxBackendRunsDockerInsideTheSandbox"" is the one that runs
  the harness for real on this backend and asserts the four claims
  ""docker: sbx"" makes: the sbx line was printed (not the fallback), the
  workspace mount carries writes back to the host, ""docker version"" INSIDE the
  sandbox reaches a daemon, and the sandbox is gone afterwards. It drives
  ""--shell"", so it costs no model call and no credential.
end note
note bottom of SBX
  **One pinned CLI surface.** ""sbx"" is pre-GA (v0.35), so every flag it takes
  is encoded in exactly four places — ""RunArgs"", ""RemoveArgs"",
  ""SecretSetArgs"", ""WriteKit"" — and callers stay declarative. Drift against
  the tool then costs one edit in one package rather than a sweep through
  ""cmd/proveo"".

  Reference docs:
  | ""https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/install/""        | platform gate + standalone install
  | ""https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/usage/""          | run / exec / cp / ports / policy / secret
  | ""https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/customize/kits/"" | Kit spec.yaml
end note

note bottom of KIT
  **""WriteKit"" returns the directory, not the file.** ""--kit"" takes a
  directory (or a ZIP), while the rendered document is ""«dir»/spec\.yaml"".
  Returning the path to the file invited exactly one bug — handing ""--kit"" a
  ""spec\.yaml"" — so the function returns the value the flag wants and the
  caller has nothing left to get wrong. The rendered file is ""0600"": it holds
  no secret values, but the posture it declares is private.
end note

note bottom of SEL
  **Purity split.** ""sandboxSpec"" is a pure function of ""runSandboxInput"":
  same input, same Kit + argv + secret list, no side effects — which is what
  makes ""--print"" and the unit tests able to assert the whole invocation
  without a sandbox. Every effect lives in ""runSandbox"": render the Kit,
  hydrate the forwarded host env, ""sbx secret set"", exec, then ""sbx rm"" the
  VM, its images and its volumes on the way out.
end note

note right of SEC
  **Credential posture follows the harness, not the backend.**

  | ""--credentials broker"" (claudecode's default) | ""sbx secret set"" host-side; the name is listed in the Kit's ""credentialsEnv"" and the value never enters argv, the env, or the VM filesystem |
  | ""--credentials forward"" (cursor's only mode)  | a **bare** ""-e NAME"" — ""sbx"" copies the value from the host environment, so it still never rides argv |

  cursor cannot use the brokered path at all: it pins TLS to "".cursor\.sh"" /
  "".cursor\.com"", so header injection has nothing to inject into. Forwarding
  on the sandbox backend therefore has to match what the docker path already
  does for it, or cursor would reach the agent with no usable key — the
  parity break that kept the harness second-class here.
end note

@enduml
